O Encheirídion de Epicteto — Dinucci e Julien (@greek-source-epictetus-pt: 0, is #book, #part-of @greek-portuguese-editions) { r_0T9SP89H4SNVSN6XV25QY7EF9W
Epicteto. Apresentação e tradução de Aldo Lopes Dinucci e Alfredo Julien. O Encheirídion de Epicteto, Archai, n. 9, 2012, pp. 50–60. Portuguese.

[Open translation and repository licensing statement](https://ri.ufs.br/handle/riufs/742). The UFS item identifies a Creative Commons Attribution licence.

**Read with:** [Epictetus: judgment, agency, and what depends on us](../schools/Epictetus.lingua#r_35EWPVCFYNWZ0DYG5R5HM05TC2). Read the same Manual sections named by the guide, then the full text. Compare what depends on us, judgments, desires, and duties with [George Long's English translation](Epictetus-Long.lingua#r_5VCYFDR3KPWTJ3T35X5MW4T4BD); cite the numbered section and translator when explaining a difference.

Keep the presentation distinct from Epictetus' translated text. The article provides a translation of the short work, not a requirement to substitute commentary for the argument.

